# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots DVGA (gevent server on :5013) in the background with
# its default insecure posture and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * DVGA is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, making the "patched the
#     source but never restarted the server" case detectable (gevent does not
#     re-import core/middleware.py per request);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting DVGA cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART DVGA, not merely start it if
# absent - it is already up with the vulnerable middleware loaded.
